 "subject": "graph,pkg,cli,mcp: remove embedding-based semantic search",
 "body": "Measured, not assumed: 15 hand-verified concept queries across 5 real\ncorpora (gin, flask, guava, typeorm, django), targets confirmed by\nreading the source, comparing two ACTUAL code paths (no LLM):\n\n  lexical  = one agent-guessed keyword -> Search (substring, ranked)\n  semantic = the full task sentence    -> SemanticSearch (Model2Vec/TF-IDF)\n\nlexical won or tied semantic on 12/15 cases, often by a wide margin\n(rank 1 vs rank 19+). Semantic won cleanly once \u2014 a query with no\nsingle-word guess at all \u2014 and even there landed at rank 3, not rank\n1. An LLM agent already IS the semantic layer: it knows domain\nvocabulary, and one guessed keyword through substring search beats an\nembedding index searching the raw sentence.\n\nRemoved: CodeGraph.SemanticSearch/newSemanticEngine and the\nsem{Mu,Engine,Dirty,VecCache} fields; Engine.Query/Engine.Semantic and\nthe Scored type from the public API; `grove query` (CLI) and\n`grove_query` (MCP tool); the internal/embeddings package entire,\nincluding its 29MB embedded Model2Vec weights (repo -29MB). Search\n(lexical, substring-ranked) is untouched and is now the only retrieval\nsurface Engine exposes \u2014 a caller with no candidate name should derive\none (g",
